WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.601
-My first guest tonight
is a very funny

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.836
and talented actor.
He voices one of the characters

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:06.339
in the new animated series
"The Great North,"

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:10.109
which you can see Sundays
at 8:30 p.m., on Fox.

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:13.412
Here's Nick Offerman,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:15.515
Ah, it is great
to see you, buddy.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.984
-Nick --
-Hello. The, uh --

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:21.420
Hang on.
Let's let the applause die down.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.790
All right. Go ahead, Jimmy.
-We can put it in post.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:29.195
Nick, it's good to see you.
Last time we talked on our show,

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:31.397
you were on the set of
"Making it,"

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:35.835
your reality show, which will
be back on NBC in June.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:40.005
And since then, you've also
filmed this series for Netflix

00:00:40.005 --> 00:00:43.442
with Ava DuVernay.
You're a busy, busy, man.

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:45.245
How does it feel to be
working back on shows again?

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:48.781
-It's incredible.
But here's the thing.

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:51.183
You know, we've been
in this pandemic for a year,

00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:53.486
and we're all sort of
locked down

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.622
and sequestered in our homes.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:58.725
And so to get to go to work
and shoot, you know,

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:01.794
an eight-episode season
of something

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:04.631
and look at a crew
of 200 people,

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:07.400
all wearing masks
and face shields

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.904
and getting tested every day,
which allows us to work

00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:14.840
and for, you know,
a couple of months at a time

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:19.479
and get this work done and pay
our rent and feed our families,

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:23.782
I just am filled with such
gratitude toward the people

00:01:23.782 --> 00:01:26.685
that are behaving like grown-ups
and saying, "Okay.

00:01:26.685 --> 00:01:29.189
This is, like --
This is an inconvenience.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:30.723
e have to wear this stuff."

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:34.227
But if we do, we can go
to our jobs, and we can be safe

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:37.163
and we can, you know, help stop
the spread of this virus.

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.031
-I totally agree.
And it's -- it's actually --

00:01:39.031 --> 00:01:42.034
it's amazing --
everyone here, as well.

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:46.739
But it's all for entertainment,
too, and to entertain people

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.441
while we're going
through this stuff.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:51.110
So, yeah, props to everyone
who puts the work in

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:54.013
for any of this entertainment.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.614
I wanted to ask you
this question.

00:01:55.614 --> 00:01:57.483
I was going to e-mail you,

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:59.485
but I think you must've
changed your e-mail

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:03.756
or you've never given it to me.
But a few months ago,

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.224
it was announced
that break dancing

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:08.060
would become an Olympic sport
in 2024.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.996
We've talked about this
on the show before.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:11.698
You used to be a break dancer.

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:14.567
What did you think
when you saw this?

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:18.538
Well, I mean, as,
you know, an activist --

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:21.140
I don't think it's too strong
of a word --

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:25.311
my whole life has been devoted
to seeing this happen, you know,

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.813
to seeing break dancing
recognized

00:02:27.813 --> 00:02:32.118
as an international sport,
a world-class sport.

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:36.088
Break dancers are clearly the
greatest athletes on the planet.

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:41.227
And so to see my work pay off,
the work of me and my cousin,

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:43.896
Tick Tock and Flip Flop,
to see everything that --

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:49.135
-Tick Tock and -- which one was
Tick Tock and who was Flip Flop?

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:51.070
-Hilarious,
as if you don't know.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:54.440
My cousin was amazing
at doing flips,

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:58.177
so he was Flip Flop,
and I was the popper and locker,

00:02:58.177 --> 00:03:00.946
so I was Tick Tock.

00:03:00.946 --> 00:03:02.648
And, you know, I mean,
that's -- that was --

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:06.752
that was what the decades
of our youth were all about,

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:09.555
seeing break dancing
become an Olympic event.

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:13.192
So this is a big day
in my house.

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:16.228
And now we can, you know --
now we can focus on

00:03:16.228 --> 00:03:17.663
on other world problems --

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:20.399
hunger and clean water
and stuff.

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:23.101
Did you --
Did you break dance --

00:03:23.101 --> 00:03:25.772
Did you ever compete?

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:29.509
-[ Scoffs ]
Did I ever...

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:31.244
-That was the funniest joke
you laughed at

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:33.979
out of all of my jokes?
-Yeah, I --

00:03:33.979 --> 00:03:36.482
I did compete, Jimmy,

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:41.521
at the Shannahan Skating Rink.
Two times we competed,

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:44.524
and one of the times,
we got third place.

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:47.793
So, yeah, you could say,
you know,

00:03:47.793 --> 00:03:51.597
that I'm a lauded break dancer.

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:54.300
I'm a decorated break dancer.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.602
-Wow, that's unbelievable.

00:03:56.602 --> 00:03:59.939
I want to talk to you
about "The Great North."

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:03.409
This is from the creators
of "Bob's Burgers,"

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:07.112
and they chose
the right man for the role.

00:04:07.112 --> 00:04:11.651
I do love your voice.
There's a character named Beef

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.786
who doesn't necessarily
look like you,

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:16.856
but he also does not
not look like you.

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:18.891
But here's a photo of Beef.

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.626
-I feel it.
-Yeah.

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:23.061
How much input did you have
in creating this character?

00:04:23.061 --> 00:04:26.532
-Well, no --
Zero direct input,

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:29.302
but I've known the creators
for a long time.

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:31.470
-Oh, there you go.
-Wendy and --

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.906
Wendy and Lizzie Molyneaux
are two sisters.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.841
That write for "Bob's Burgers."

00:04:35.841 --> 00:04:38.511
And Wendy's husband,
Jeff Drake, is also very funny.

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:41.147
And Megan actually met them.

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:45.952
You probably met them and
didn't know it a long time ago.

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:49.288
They used to write promos
for NBC.

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:52.925
And so Megan met them,
and she had a talk show

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:56.062
on NBC a while ago.
-Yep.

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:58.864
-And so she hired them
to write on her talk show.

00:04:58.864 --> 00:05:01.100
And we all started
screwing around together.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:04.270
And -- And so...

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:07.840
You know, by that,
you can deduce that Megan and I

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:10.142
are responsible for
"Bob's Burgers"

00:05:10.142 --> 00:05:15.981
and "The Simpsons"
and really all of Fox Animation.

00:05:15.981 --> 00:05:17.617
You can trace it back to us.
-Yeah.

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:22.855
-[ Laughs ]
-The character Beef

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:26.358
is the captain
of a fishing boat in Alaska.

00:05:26.358 --> 00:05:28.460
It's very, very funny.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:30.829
Do you fish?
I'm assuming you fish.

00:05:30.829 --> 00:05:34.233
Have you ever been chased
by wild dogs while fishing?

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:37.770
-I never have.
There is a lot of wildlife.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.573
We go to Minnesota
every summer, and --

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:42.975
-Timberwolves?

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:44.544
-They're probably --

00:05:44.544 --> 00:05:47.480
There are timberwolves
and coyotes around,

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:50.916
but they know better
than to mess with my family.

00:05:50.916 --> 00:05:54.753
My sisters
are very intimidating.

00:05:54.753 --> 00:05:57.523
One is a librarian
and one is a schoolteacher.

00:05:57.523 --> 00:06:01.060
And especially when I go
to the national parks

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:05.064
where there's bears,
I bring my sisters, and those --

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:07.433
You know, we've seen bears
approaching from a distance,

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:10.002
and they're like,
"The Offerman girls?

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:13.038
No, thank you, sir,"
and they run the other way.

00:06:13.038 --> 00:06:15.607
"The Great North" is picked up
for a second season.

00:06:15.607 --> 00:06:17.209
Congratulations on that.

00:06:17.209 --> 00:06:20.079
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's the very funny

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:22.081
Nick Offerman
in "The Great North."

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:23.382
Take a look at this.

00:06:23.382 --> 00:06:25.450
-Whoa!
-Dad, you could've died!

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:27.486
Or ripped the banner.
-What's all this about?

00:06:27.486 --> 00:06:28.754
-Brian called last night.

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:30.790
He's coming up from Anchorage
for the weekend

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.926
to have dinner with a client.
-Uncle Brian's coming? Sick!

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:35.528
-It is very sick.

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:37.062
And I want everything
to be perfect.

00:06:37.062 --> 00:06:39.498
It's been a full year since
he moved to that urban hellhole

00:06:39.498 --> 00:06:41.100
to launch his hot-tub business.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.869
Poor guy. I'm sure he can't wait
to hang out with me

00:06:43.869 --> 00:06:46.472
and do all our old favorite
activities, like fishing

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:49.374
and then talking about
how fishing went.

00:06:49.374 --> 00:06:52.144
-Nick Offerman, everybody.
"The Great North" airs Sundays

00:06:52.144 --> 00:06:55.447
at 8:30 p.m., on Fox.
There he is, the creator

00:06:55.447 --> 00:06:58.251
of all of Fox Animation,
Nick Offerman.

